infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Top-3 orders per user: N+1 loop vs one LATERAL query
  desc Same result for 800 users — the rewrite the lesson clocks at 4 s to 90 ms
  compares
    - label N+1 application loop
      children
        - label 800 queries
          desc One round trip per user, fired from app code
        - label ~4000 ms endpoint
          desc Measured for 800 users
        - label Repeated scans
          desc Each user's orders fetched in a separate call
    - label Single LATERAL query
      children
        - label 1 query
          desc CROSS JOIN LATERAL (... ORDER BY ... LIMIT 3)
        - label ~90 ms endpoint
          desc About 44x faster, sub-100 ms
        - label Indexed nested loop
          desc Inner LIMIT 3 reads ~3 index entries per user
